bext is a multi-crate project. The engine is free software under the GNU
Affero General Public License v3.0; most of the rest of the repository is
MIT-licensed. A commercial license is available for the engine as an
alternative to the AGPL.

  MIT (default):
    Applies to every crate and package in this repository EXCEPT those listed
    below. The MIT text appears further down in this file.

  GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 only (AGPL-3.0-only):
    Applies to the following engine crates. Each crate ships its own
    LICENSE.md; the full AGPL-3.0 text is in LICENSE-AGPL-3.0 at the root of
    this repository and at https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.txt.

        - crates/bext-core         (routing, SSR, caching, flow engine)
        - crates/bext-plugin       (plugin orchestration and lifecycle)
        - crates/bext-v8           (V8 SSR eval engine)
        - crates/bext-server       (HTTP server runtime and vhost dispatcher)
        - crates/bext-proxy        (reverse-proxy subsystem of bext-server)
        - crates/bext-waf          (web application firewall)
        - crates/bext-tls          (TLS termination and ACME)
        - crates/bext-nginx-compat (nginx config parser, drop-in replacement)
        - crates/bext-nginx-shim   (nginx CLI translator)
        - crates/bext-lite         (minimal QuickJS runtime for AOT-exported PRISM apps)
        - crates/bext-lite-desktop (desktop shell for bext-lite)

    In short: you may run, study, modify and redistribute these crates. If
    you distribute them, or let users interact with a modified version over a
    network, you must offer those users the corresponding source code of your
    version under the AGPL-3.0. Applications served by the engine are not
    covered by this requirement merely because the engine serves them.

  Commercial license:
    The copyright holder offers the engine crates under a separate commercial
    license for uses that cannot meet the AGPL-3.0 conditions, such as
    embedding the engine in a closed-source product or offering a modified
    engine as a hosted service without publishing the changes. See
    https://bext.dev/partners or open an issue at
    https://github.com/bext-stack/bext/issues.

  Closed source:
    The following crates are NOT distributed under any public license and
    are not published to any registry. They remain the private property of
    the copyright holder:
      - crates/bext-license
      - crates/bext-keygen

